      "id": 1,
      "text": "Arjay sprang up as a planned coal town in the early 1900s, thanks to the Louisville & Nashville Railroad’s arrival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arjay_kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the initials of coal operator R., a key figure in its early development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
