      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arjay%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Arjay’s post office opened on February 23, 1911, with George W. Hairston as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arjay_kentucky",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coal mining in Arjay peaked during the 1920s through 1940s, driven by wartime demand and industrial growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arjay_kentucky",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By the mid‑1950s, many Straight Creek valley mines near Arjay closed as reserves ran out, leaving abandoned camps.",
